   "id": "claim_p_b13",
   "type": "claim",
   "label": "P-B13: not supported",
   "description": "Sealed before the run was acquired: 400 µm at air display 3: a quarter of B6 (inverse thickness, if still thermally thin). Ratio below the band; the interval (0.09–0.37, with the reference run's own uncertainty) does not exclude it. The edge of the 400 µm flame is broad and flickering (r² 0.42 at the 0.5 reference), and the air display flickers between 3 and 2 inside the segment. Other airflow settings in the same run give 0.42–0.77 mm/s; the registered segment is kept. The verdict depends on the front definition fixed beforehand (0.5 of peak): at 0.05, 0.1 and 0.2 of peak the ratio is 0.25, 0.26 and 0.23, inside the band (RES-039). No explanation is claimed: the thin-fuel check finds no sign that this run alone became thermally thick (RES-043), and the table does not name its material as PMMA.",
